{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"impudent-sodium-ferret","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# New-gate CI steps fail pre-gate changes: workflow from target branch, tree from change\n\n## Summary\n\nGerrit's verify job takes the **workflow definition from the target branch** but **checks out the change's tree**. A newly landed gate step that runs a repo script (`python scripts/check_X.py`) therefore hard-fails every open change whose base predates the gate-introducing commit: the step runs, but the script does not exist in the checked-out tree.\n\nObserved in production: changes 1332/1333 (based before d37e's 6739ea54fa landed) failed Verified with `python: can't open file '.../scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory`. The just-merged wall-clock-assert gate (1e95, 9af88c3ada, scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py) has the identical window. Immediate recovery for 1332/1333 was a server-side rebase:chain — but every future gate-script landing re-opens this window for all in-flight changes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe two new gate steps in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml invoke their script unconditionally. The workflow definition and the checked-out tree can legitimately diverge (definition-from-target-branch is Gerrit CI's model), so a gate step must tolerate a tree that predates its script.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nGuard both new gate steps with an existence check that SKIPS (with an explanatory log line) when the script is absent from the checked-out tree:\n\n    - name: raw-git-write gate\n      run: |\n        if [ -f scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py ]; then\n          python scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py\n        else\n          echo \"scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py not in checked-out tree (change predates the gate) — skipping\"\n        fi\n\nSame shape for the wall-clock-assert gate step. Include an inline workflow comment stating the idiom and WHY (definition-from-target-branch vs change tree skew), so future gate authors copy the guard along with the step. Deleting a gate script in a change silently skips that gate for that change — acceptable: such a deletion is itself visible in review, and the gate re-enforces on every post-merge change.\n\nOlder gate steps (comment-hygiene, module-size, commit wrap) predate all open changes; leave them unguarded to keep the diff minimal — the documented idiom covers any future script.\n\n## Verification\n\n- actionlint via make lint passes on the edited workflow.\n- Shell logic locally exercised both branches: script present -> runs detector (exit propagates); script absent (temp dir) -> skip message, exit 0.\n- CI on the change itself (which HAS both scripts) still runs both gates — Verified +1 proves the present-branch path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both new gate steps (raw-git-write, wall-clock-assert) skip with an explanatory message when their script is absent from the checked-out tree, and run it when present.\n- [ ] The skew rationale + copy-me idiom is documented inline in the workflow at the gate steps.\n- [ ] make lint (actionlint) passes; both branches of the guard exercised locally.\n\n## File impact\n\n- .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml (edit)","id":"ee2a-c7d7-3d73-425e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"New-gate CI steps fail pre-gate changes: workflow from target branch, tree from change"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785807684044955001,"uuid":"e8d0374a-3ee5-42c9-97bf-008070314445"}